DESIGN NOTES (faithful + in-scope decisions)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Data source: the page binds to the SHARED, already-wired S8 feed
  AnalyticsStore.weeklyDigest(vehicleId) → GET /vehicles/{id}/weekly-digest
  (internal/api/weeklydigest/handler.go), documented in the store as the web
  `useWeeklyDigest` port. This is the in-scope analogue of the web hook's reads
  (DataContainer exposes analyticsStore + vehiclesStore + settingsStore +
  selectedVehicleStore; it does NOT expose driving/charging stores and is NOT in
  this artifact's allowed files, so the rendered server aggregate is used — exactly
  the LifetimeStatsPage precedent). The three data states are genuine cache-then-
  network Resource phases projected through ResourceUiState.toUiState (ADR-013),
  never fabricated.
* hasData gate: WeeklyDigest.hasData = drives>0 || distanceKm>0 || energyKwh>0
  mirrors the web `weekDrives.length||weekCharging.length` empty gate, so an
  all-zero week — or a vehicle-less fleet (via toNoVehicleDigest) — resolves to
  UiPhase.Empty (the web `noData`/`noDataMessage` EmptyState).
* SI-canonical (Phase-48): distance read as km off the wire, converted at the
  display boundary only via prefs.fromKm → convertDistanceFromSI(km*1000, unit);
  energy(kWh)/efficiency(Wh/km) keep the canonical display units the web renders.
* Strings: 4 of 5 keys pre-existed in res/values*/strings.xml. The missing
  translation_analytics_weeklyDigest_noDataMessage was added to all three locale
  catalogs (values, values-ar, values-he — ar/he ship the English fallback per
  the generated-catalog convention, app/lint.xml note (1)).
* Navigation: the `weeklyDigest`/`/weekly-digest` destination already exists in
  Destinations.kt (NavGroup.Analytics); a PageHost + one idempotent register()
  call in TeslaSyncApplication attach the screen (LifetimeStatsPageHost precedent).
* Tests: a co-located unit test would live under app/src/test/** which is OUTSIDE
  this artifact's allowed files (the sibling analytics LifetimeStatsPage has none
  either); decode/format/trend logic is isolated in the framework-free model and
  the full :android:testDebugUnitTest suite passes (TEST_EXIT=0 below).

